.TH APKG.CONF 5 "October 2026" "apkg 0.3.4" "Amix File Formats"
.SH NAME
apkg.conf \- configuration file of the apkg package client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/apkg.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR apkg (1)
reads
.B /etc/apkg.conf
(or the file named with
.BR "apkg \-c" )
at start.  Each line is
.IB key = value\fR;
a line starting with
.B #
is a comment, and blank lines are ignored.  A key the file does not name
takes its built-in default, so the file only needs the keys you change.
.PP
The file is a
.BR conffile (5)
of the APKG package: an upgrade keeps your edited file and puts the new
default beside it as
.BR /etc/apkg.conf.new .
The default of the installed version is also always readable as
.BR /usr/apkg/lib/apkg.conf .
.SH KEYS
Each key, its default and its full meaning are in
.BR apkg (1),
section CONFIGURATION.
.TP 18
.B repo
repository base URL (http://pkg.amigaux.org)
.TP
.B cachedir
package download cache (/var/apkg/cache)
.TP
.B pkgadd\fR, \fBpkgrm
the engine binaries (/usr/apkg/bin/pkgadd, /usr/apkg/bin/pkgrm, falling
back to /usr/sbin)
.TP
.B admin
the
.BR admin (5)
file for pkgadd and pkgrm (/var/apkg/admin)
.TP
.B kbootset\fR, \fBkbootset_journal
the generation composer run after a kernel-space transaction, and its
journal
.TP
.B timeout\fR, \fBconnect_timeout
seconds of silence on a transfer, and for a connect
.TP
.B retries\fR, \fBretry_delay
further attempts of a failed fetch, and the seconds between them
.TP
.B progress
progress output during a download
.TP
.B bufsize\fR, \fBrcvbuf\fR, \fBsndbuf
the transfer buffer and the socket buffer sizes
.TP
.B redirects
how many HTTP redirects to follow
.TP
.B nameserver
a DNS server to ask when
.B /etc/inet/hosts
has no answer (repeatable)
.TP
.B dns_timeout\fR, \fBdns_retries
seconds per DNS query attempt, and further attempts per nameserver
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
# apkg configuration
repo=http://pkg.amigaux.org
cachedir=/var/apkg/cache
admin=/var/apkg/admin
nameserver=192.0.2.53
.fi
.SH FILES
.PD 0
.TP 28
.B /etc/apkg.conf
this file
.TP
.B /etc/apkg.conf.new
the new default after an upgrade that kept your file
.TP
.B /usr/apkg/lib/apkg.conf
the default of the installed version (not read by apkg)
.PD
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apkg (1),
.BR admin (5),
.BR conffile (5)
